## 4. Key Business Insights

### 4.1 Employee Attrition

A total of 237 employees left the organization out of 1,470 employees.

The calculated attrition rate is 16.12%.

This metric provides an overview of employee turnover within the organization.

### 4.2 Active Workforce

The organization has 1,233 active employees, representing the remaining workforce in the dataset.

### 4.3 Average Employee Income

The overall average employee income is 6,502.93.

The average income of employees who left is 4,787.09.

This difference can be investigated further to understand possible relationships between compensation and employee attrition.

### 4.4 Department-Wise Attrition

The Sales department recorded 92 employees who left.

This makes department-level employee retention an important area for further investigation.

### 4.5 Overtime and Attrition

A total of 127 employees who left were identified in the overtime analysis.

This observation can be explored further to understand the relationship between overtime and employee turnover.

## 5. Recommendations

- Monitor employee attrition regularly.
- Investigate department-wise employee turnover.
- Examine compensation patterns among employees who leave.
- Evaluate overtime distribution and employee retention.
- Monitor employee satisfaction and work-life balance.

## 6. Conclusion

The analysis provides an overview of employee attrition, workforce strength, income, and tenure.

The findings can help HR teams identify areas that require further investigation and support data-driven workforce planning.